<h3>The question each level answers</h3>
<div class="scn-board">
    <div class="scn-card">
        <h4>Find exactly</h4>
        <div class="scn-meta"><span class="scn-pill lv1">Level 1</span><span class="scn-pill">Files · routing</span></div>
        <p class="scn-body"><strong>"That word or file I wrote &mdash; where is it?"</strong> &mdash; you point straight at it with a <code>CLAUDE.md</code> acting as a router plus a folder structure.</p>
        <p class="scn-sub">When &mdash; when you re-explain often and search by exact name</p>
    </div>
    <div class="scn-card">
        <h4>Group by topic</h4>
        <div class="scn-meta"><span class="scn-pill lv2">Level 2</span><span class="scn-pill">Wiki · memory</span></div>
        <p class="scn-body"><strong>"Gather everything about this topic."</strong> &mdash; you walk down the LLM wiki's index and weave the related notes together.</p>
        <p class="scn-sub">When &mdash; 30+ notes and you keep forgetting what you had</p>
    </div>
    <div class="scn-card">
        <h4>Find by meaning</h4>
        <div class="scn-meta"><span class="scn-pill lv3">Level 3</span><span class="scn-pill">Vector · embedding</span></div>
        <p class="scn-body"><strong>"Find something close in meaning even if the words differ."</strong> &mdash; semantic search (a vector DB) looks at similarity by meaning.</p>
        <p class="scn-sub">When &mdash; when notes that exist get missed over word mismatches</p>
    </div>
    <div class="scn-card">
        <h4>Connect by relationship</h4>
        <div class="scn-meta"><span class="scn-pill lv4">Level 4</span><span class="scn-pill">Knowledge graph</span></div>
        <p class="scn-body"><strong>"Start at X and follow the connections to A."</strong> &mdash; you trace chains of relationships through a knowledge graph of entities and relations.</p>
        <p class="scn-sub">When &mdash; when "who is tangled with what, and how" matters</p>
    </div>
    <div class="scn-card">
        <h4>Autonomous brain OS</h4>
        <div class="scn-meta"><span class="scn-pill lv5">Level 5</span><span class="scn-pill">always-on</span></div>
        <p class="scn-body"><strong>"Stay updated on your own without me minding it."</strong> &mdash; an always-on brain that keeps absorbing meetings, mail, and memos automatically (cron).</p>
        <p class="scn-sub">When &mdash; when offline agents or bulk data need constant syncing</p>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="note warn">
    <span class="nh">The most important principle</span>
    Choose <strong>the lowest level that matches your pain</strong>. If nothing is uncomfortable right now, there is no reason to climb. And <strong>the level may differ from folder to folder even within a single project</strong> &mdash; meeting minutes at level 3, the project folder at level 1, for instance.
</div>

